<title>UK: TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDAL WINNERS.</title>
<headline>TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDAL WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medal winners at the world table tennis championships ending on Monday:</p>
<p>Men's singles</p>
<p>Gold - Jan-Ove Waldner (Sweden)</p>
<p>Silver - Vladimir Samsonov (Belarus)</p>
<p>Women's singles</p>
<p>Gold - Deng Yaping (China)</p>
<p>Silver - Wang Nan (China)</p>
<p>Men's doubles</p>
<p>Gold - Kong Linghui/Liu Guoliang (China)</p>
<p>Silver - Jan-Ove Waldner/Jorgen Persson (Sweden)</p>
<p>Women's doubles</p>
<p>Gold - Deng Yaping/Yang Ying (China)</p>
<p>Silver - Li Ju/Wang Nan (China) Mixed doubles</p>
<p>Gold - Liu Guoliang/Wu Na (China)</p>
<p>Silver - Kong Linghui/Deng Yaping (China)</p>
<p>Men's team - China</p>
<p>Women's team - China</p>
</text>
